# Hassan Orders dashboard parity (web ↔ Android)

Marker: `ORDERS_APP_DASHBOARD_PARITY_LOCKED` (`scripts/verifyOrdersApp.js` on build).

When changing **Hassan Awad’s quotationer dashboard** (web sidebar under quotationer-only UX) or the **Orders** mobile app:

1. Read **`docs/hassan-orders-dashboard-parity.md`**.
2. Update **`src/mobile/ordersAppDashboardParity.js`** first, then copy to **`mobile-apps/shared/ordersAppDashboardParity.js`**.
3. Wire **web** (`AppChrome` uses `buildQuotationerOnlyNavGroups`) and **mobile** (`DashboardScreen` + `App.js` stacks) from that module — do not hand-edit nav/tile lists elsewhere.
4. Keep **`ORDERS_APP_SCREENS`**, **`HASSAN_AWAD.allowedRoutes`**, screen implementations, and **API handlers** aligned so behaviour matches, not just labels.
5. Run **`node scripts/verifyOrdersApp.js`** before finishing.

Forbidden without updating parity + mobile + verify: adding a Hassan sidebar item or Orders dashboard tile in only one place.
